## 👨‍💻 About Me

I'm a cybersecurity professional working as a **SOC Analyst at Zscaler**, focused on security monitoring, threat detection, incident investigation, and defensive security operations.

I enjoy investigating suspicious activity, understanding attacker techniques, improving detection logic, and exploring automation to make security operations more effective.

My long-term goal is to grow into a **Security Engineer**, combining detection engineering, digital forensics, threat hunting, and security automation.

- 🛡️ **Role:** Security Operations Center Analyst
- 🔍 **Focus:** Threat Detection, Incident Response & Threat Hunting
- 📊 **SIEM:** Wazuh
- 🧠 **Framework:** MITRE ATT&CK
- 🕵️ **Interests:** DFIR, Malware Analysis & Threat Intelligence
- ⚙️ **Direction:** Detection Engineering & SOC Automation

---

## 🛡️ Security Expertise

| Area | Focus |
|---|---|
| **SOC Operations** | Alert triage, event correlation, incident investigation |
| **Detection Engineering** | Detection logic, SIEM rule tuning, false-positive reduction |
| **Threat Hunting** | Suspicious behavior analysis, attacker TTPs, threat hypotheses |
| **Incident Response** | Alert validation, root-cause analysis, containment coordination |
| **Digital Forensics** | Endpoint investigation, evidence analysis, forensic workflows |
| **Threat Intelligence** | OSINT, IOC analysis, threat-context enrichment |
| **Malware Analysis** | Static and behavioral analysis of suspicious files |
| **Network Security** | TCP/IP, DNS, HTTP/HTTPS, IDS/IPS, firewalls, WAF |
| **Security Automation** | Alert enrichment, repetitive task automation, workflow improvement |

